EXT. SKI GONDOLA - MIDWAY - DUSK

A six-seat gondola cabin dangling in the blue hour, stalled between two pylons over a canyon of pines. Wind taps the glass. Snow dusts the roof. The cable above is dead still.

Inside, five people sit in silence, knees almost touching.

RAVENNA OKONKWO-DALE (40s, ski patrol jacket, radio on her chest) watches the pylon. LORENZO BIANCHI-RAO (60s, fur-trimmed parka, fake smile) clutches a thermos. KWAME ASANTE (20s, snowboarder, beanie, headphones) stares at his boots. LOTTE HOLMGREN (30s, ski instructor, red jacket) cradles her phone.  And in the corner, curled around a school backpack, PEARL WAKEFIELD (10, pink helmet, wide eyes) hugs her knees.

Nobody speaks. The cabin sways once, then holds.

RAVENNA
Everybody stay seated.

LORENZO
We are seated.

RAVENNA
I'm saying it so it's said.

The radio on her chest crackles. CONTROL (V.O.) comes through, flat and distant.

CONTROL (V.O.)
(over radio)
Gondola Seven, this is Base. We have a generator fault. Estimated restart forty minutes.

RAVENNA
(into radio)
Copy, Base. We have five on board, one minor.

CONTROL (V.O.)
(over radio)
Copy. Keep them calm.

Ravenna lowers the radio. Looks around. Everyone has heard.

LOTTE
Forty minutes.

KWAME
Forty minutes is nothing.

LORENZO
It is cold.

Pearl lifts her head.

PEARL
Can I have my mom?

Lotte reaches across. Pearl shrinks back, then lets her take one hand.

LOTTE
Hey. I'm Lotte. I teach kids how to ski.

PEARL
I'm not good.

LOTTE
Nobody's good at first.

Lorenzo unscrews the thermos. Pours a little into the cap. Offers it to Pearl. Ravenna intercepts.

RAVENNA
Cocoa?

LORENZO
Brandy.

RAVENNA
No.

LORENZO
It is only a little.

RAVENNA
She's ten.

He sighs and drinks it himself. Kwame watches the pylon; the wind picks up and the cabin rocks. Everyone grabs a bar, a seat, a knee. Pearl yelps.

The rocking eases. A hush falls. Kwame lowers his head and begins to hum, low, tuneless. One by one, they listen.

LOTTE
(softly)
That's nice. Keep going.

Lorenzo shifts. His fur collar rustles. He leans forward and, for the first time, speaks without the smile.

LORENZO
I am afraid of heights.

Nobody answers. Ravenna lays a hand on his knee. Kwame removes one earbud and offers it to Pearl without looking.

Pearl hesitates, then puts it in. Her eyes widen.

PEARL
It's loud.

KWAME
Yeah.

PEARL
I like it.

Something clanks overhead. All five look up. A wire hums. The gondola shudders, then drops six inches and catches.

Pearl screams. Lotte grabs her. Lorenzo grips the bar. Kwame's humming rises.

RAVENNA
(into radio)
Base! Base, we just dropped!

CONTROL (V.O.)
(over radio)
Gondola Seven, say again?

RAVENNA
We dropped six inches!

CONTROL (V.O.)
(over radio)
Copy. Stand by.

The cabin trembles. Nobody breathes.

The cable twitches. A creak runs down it like a bowstring. The gondola lurches forward, one foot, two, then stops again.

KWAME
We're moving.

LOTTE
We're moving!

Kwame's humming swells. Lorenzo closes his eyes. Pearl takes out the earbud and hands it back, solemn.

PEARL
Thanks.

KWAME
Anytime.

The gondola glides, smooth and certain, down toward the lights of the valley.

Ravenna lowers the radio. Closes her eyes. Exhales for the first time in forty minutes.
